  - The minimum task and user model the above requires

  [1mExplicitly deferred, named so nothing blocks them later[0m
  - Email, real-time push, web push (the delivery interface leaves room; nothing else does)
  - Per-user notification preferences beyond mute-per-task
  - Digesting and rate limits — these arrive [3mwith[0m email, not before, since the in-app feed doesn't need them
  - Teams, projects, permissions beyond "authenticated users share one task list"

  [1mBuild order[0m — four plans, each shippable:
  1. Tasks + auth (the floor: a task list several people can log into and edit)
  2. Event log (task writes emit events; activity history visible on a task)
  3. Subscriptions (auto-subscribe rules, watch/mute button)
  4. Notifications (fan-out, feed, unread count)

  Notifications are plan 4 of 4. I want to be direct that plans 1–3 are most of the work, and that asking for "a
  notifications system" is buying all four.

  Alongside that, a tooling question — this is the cheapest it will ever be, since no code exists yet.

